@startuml domain-model
' Report §2.4 — the whole domain model at class-name level: one package per bounded context
' plus common-events as the Published Language. Attributes and operations are in the
' per-context diagrams (domain-programme, -registration, -billing, -access, -assistance,
' -published-language), which include exactly the same source fragments as this one.
' New classes go in the include/domain-*.iuml fragments and new event links in
' include/domain-event-links.iuml.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
hide members
left to right direction
hide empty members

title Converge — domain model overview (bounded contexts and Published Language)

!$overview = "true"
!include include/domain-programme.iuml
!include include/domain-registration.iuml
!include include/domain-billing.iuml
!include include/domain-access.iuml
!include include/domain-assistance.iuml
!include include/domain-insight.iuml
!include include/domain-published-language.iuml
!include include/domain-event-links.iuml

' White links (Smetana ignores hidden and transparent ones) only stagger the contexts into two columns.
Event -[#FFFFFF]-> Registration
PaymentOrder -[#FFFFFF]-> Ticket
ClashDetector -[#FFFFFF]-> FillRate

legend right
  <b>Reading this diagram</b>
  «AggregateRoot», «Entity», «ValueObject», «DomainService»,
  «ReadModel», «DomainEvent», «Port»: DDD roles of each class
  filled-diamond line: composition inside an aggregate
  solid arrow: association to an enumeration-typed attribute
  dashed arrow "by id only": a reference across aggregates
  Every Published Language record implements DomainEvent:
  topic = eventType(), key = partitionKey().
  <b>Events are not drawn here.</b> Which aggregate publishes
  and which reacts to each Published Language record is in the
  per-context figures (domain-programme, -registration,
  -billing, -access, -insight, -published-language).
  Attendee assistance has no events: it reads other contexts
  over REST. Nothing crosses a context boundary except the
  Published Language records.
endlegend
@enduml
